# 101 (found 2026-10-07 running the annotations suite, G12 phase 9): a
# rider on a disjunction's member is held, and the hash form shows it,
# but the canon writes the member without it, so a canon read back
# loses the annotation. deprecate() has done the same since G3. Both
# ports agree, so this is not a parity defect.
#
# expected: {"a":meta(1,{"title":"T"})|2}
# actual:   {"a":1|2}
# run: node ../../ts/bin/aontu.js --canon disjunct-member-canon.aontu
a: meta(1, {title: "T"}) | 2
